Scaffold the Expo app on SDK 57

Phase 0: the app builds, typechecks, lints, and tests clean, with no product
feature implemented. Structure follows docs/architecture/client.md rather than
the default template.

Navigation is the five tabs the founder fixed on 2026-08-13, and the deep-link
routes from PRD 16 exist as real route definitions so a shared link and the
in-app screen cannot drift apart.

Two guardrails are wired up because the design review found defects that would
otherwise have shipped, and discipline alone would not have caught them:

- A lint rule bans colour literals outside src/ui/tokens, so a hardcoded hex
  cannot reintroduce the contrast defect design-system.md opens with.
- A contrast test computes WCAG ratios for every permitted foreground and pins
  each to the value printed in the design tables. It also asserts Amber and
  Sage still fail on Parchment, so the fills-never-ink rule cannot be quietly
  undone. It immediately caught two ratios rounded wrongly by hand: Ink on Sage
  is 6.1 not 6.2, and Ink on Stone is 4.9 not 5.0. Both still clear AA, so the
  design is unchanged and the tables are corrected.

Share-destination URL schemes are declared in the native config even though v1
routes through the OS share sheet and never calls them, since a manifest entry
cannot ship over the air.

Also resolves a stale cross-reference in design-system.md that still described
the comparison card's opponent rank as an open question after it was decided.
